<section id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <h2 id="problem-title" class="mb-8 text-3xl font-bold">Why we built it</h2>
  <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <p>
        Almost no film is cut by one person, and more teams work from different
        cities. Yet every pro editing tool treats the timeline as a one-person
        space.
      </p>
      <figure class="border-primary border-l-4 pl-4">
        <blockquote class="italic">
          "It's not currently possible for more than one editor to make changes
          on the same timeline."
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption class="opacity-70">Adobe staff, 2017. Still true.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>
        Writers got Google Docs. Designers got Figma. Developers got live pair
        programming. Film editors are still waiting for their turn.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ol class="timeline timeline-vertical timeline-compact">
      {
        [
          "Save the project file",
          "Zip and upload",
          "Message your partner",
          "Download and relink media",
          "Open it. Now they wait.",
        ].map((s, i, a) => (
          <li>
            {i > 0 && <hr />}
            <div class="timeline-middle">
              <div class="badge badge-error badge-xs" aria-hidden="true" />
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-end timeline-box">{s}</div>
            {i < a.length - 1 && <hr />}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
